<title>RUSSIA: Russian 686-day bond tranche priced 101.18 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 686-day bond tranche priced 101.18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average price on a 686-day additional tranche of Russian OFZ interest-bearing bond was 101.18 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The orginal issue on Tuesday closed at 101.35 percent to yield 22.17 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Series number		   24013</p>
<p>(additional tranche)</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		  3.39 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		     3.52 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold				2.82 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  2.94 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		   101.18 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	 101.00 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		    22.59 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	 23.08 pct</p>
<p>    Original issue date	   May 28, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor (remaining)	     686 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   May 26, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon date	     Nov 26, 1997</p>
<p>    First coupon rate	     26.63 pct</p>
<p>The first coupon will be 132,785 roubles, less accruals of 30,642.69 roubles.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry on Wednesday has raised 635.51 billion roubles by placing 1,067-day bond tranche (series 25016), taking total proceeds from the day's auctions to 3.58 trillion roubles.</p>
<p>It has also repaid 4.59 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 18-month series 24005 OFZ bond, as well as 354.39 billion roubles in interest on the bond.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
